**Finding: missing** (rule IP — Ownership of deliverables and Customer Data)

The Kubient MSA has no intellectual property article at all. The only proprietary-rights language is §14(b) (names, trademarks, logos) and the Customer warranty at §9(c)(i) that it owns the Content and Properties — neither establishes ownership as between the parties. There is nothing on:

- our rights in the Requests / visitor data flowing to Kubient (§3(g), §9(b)(iii));
- ownership of the "deliverables" and "products delivered hereunder" that Kubient's own warranties (§9(b)(i), (viii)) presuppose;
- any bar on joint ownership.

Nothing assigns our IP or data to Kubient, so this is not walk-away territory — but with no usable clause the critical ip-data rule is unmet. I inserted a short §13A confirming we retain the Content, Properties and Customer Data (with Kubient's use limited to providing the Services and no third-party disclosure), Kubient assigning Customer-specific deliverables, Kubient keeping the Auction Platform and background tools subject to a perpetual, irrevocable, royalty-free licence-back for embedded materials, and no joint ownership. The fallback (Kubient ownership of generic tools plus the perpetual sublicensable licence) is offered in the comment. Redline validated ok:true.
